---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Creations · Jake DevWorks" description="Explore Jake Ardoin’s 3D prints, magnetic designs, and plans for personalized figurines and custom T-shirts.">
  <SiteHeader article/>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="collection-intro wrap" aria-labelledby="creations-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">JAKE DEVWORKS / CREATIONS</p>
        <h1 id="creations-title">Ideas you<br>can <em>hold.</em></h1>
        <p class="collection-lead">From a first sketch to a finished piece.</p>
        <p class="collection-description">Practical 3D prints, personal projects, and a few ideas for what comes next. This is where digital designs become things you can hold, display, and wear.</p>
        <a class="button button-gold" href="#workbench">At the workbench <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
      <nav class="creation-index" aria-label="Explore creations">
        <p class="eyebrow">DESIGN → PRINT → REFINE</p>
        <a href="#trash-bag-dispenser"><span>01</span> Everyday problem-solving <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a href="#printed-business-card"><span>02</span> Branding you can hold <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a href="#mario-block-lights"><span>03</span> A little game-inspired glow <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a href="#geometric-tiger"><span>04</span> Purple & gold pride <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a href="#heygears"><span>05</span> Full Color 3D Creations <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a href="#custom-shirts"><span>06</span> Ideas you can wear <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
      </nav>
    </section>
    <section class="workbench-section section" id="workbench" aria-labelledby="workbench-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">DESIGN / PRINT / EXPERIMENT</p><h2 id="workbench-title">From the <em>workbench.</em></h2></div>
          <p>The finished pieces,<br>and the process that gets them there.</p>
        </div>
        <article class="creation-showcase" id="trash-bag-dispenser" aria-labelledby="dispenser-title">
          <figure class="creation-media creation-media-portrait">
            <picture><source srcset="/assets/creations/trash-bag-dispenser.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/assets/creations/trash-bag-dispenser.png" width="1355" height="1800" alt="Gray 3D-printed trash bag dispenser with a purple bar, JA monogram, and a bag pulled through the front" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture>
            <figcaption>A printed iteration of my trash bag dispenser.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="creation-copy"><p class="eyebrow">01 / FUNCTIONAL 3D PRINT</p><h3 id="dispenser-title">A place for the<br><em>next bag.</em></h3><p>A custom trash bag dispenser designed to keep a roll together and the next bag within reach. The gray housing, purple bar, and JA monogram give a useful everyday piece a personal finish.</p><p>The design has evolved through several iterations, with a removable hood and refinements to the spring-bar connection. The latest v6 CAD revision strengthens that connection; its spring action and long-term durability still need physical testing.</p><span class="creation-label">TRASH BAG DISPENSER / ITERATIVE DESIGN</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="creation-showcase creation-showcase-reverse" id="printed-business-card" aria-labelledby="card-title">
          <figure class="creation-media"><picture><source srcset="/assets/creations/printed-business-card.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/assets/creations/printed-business-card.png" width="1600" height="1205" alt="Jake Ardoin’s multicolor 3D-printed business card with raised logo, lettering, and service icons" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>My services, turned into something tangible.</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="creation-copy"><p class="eyebrow">02 / PRINTED BRANDING</p><h3 id="card-title">A first impression<br>with <em>dimension.</em></h3><p>A business card that shows what I do before I even start explaining it. Raised lettering, my JA logo, and icons for software development, business websites, and custom 3D prints bring the Jake DevWorks brand into the real world.</p><p>It’s a small example of how design and 3D printing can make an everyday introduction feel more personal.</p><span class="creation-label">BUSINESS CARD / MULTICOLOR 3D PRINT</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="creation-showcase creation-showcase-wide" id="mario-block-lights" aria-labelledby="mario-title">
          <div class="creation-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / PERSONAL PROJECT</p><h3 id="mario-title">A little<br><em>power-up glow.</em></h3><p>Mario-inspired question-block lights that bring a familiar bit of gaming into the room. The yellow block and raised question marks become a warm, playful focal point when the light comes on.</p><p>A fun meeting of 3D printing, nostalgia, and home decoration. These two photos show the illuminated piece from different angles.</p><span class="creation-label">QUESTION-BLOCK LIGHTS / GAME-INSPIRED DECOR</span></div>
          <div class="creation-photo-pair"><figure class="creation-media"><picture><source srcset="/assets/creations/mario-question-block.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/assets/creations/mario-question-block.png" width="1355" height="1800" alt="Close view of an illuminated yellow Mario-inspired question block mounted in a room" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>The question-block details, lit up.</figcaption></figure><figure class="creation-media"><picture><source srcset="/assets/creations/mario-question-block-room.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/assets/creations/mario-question-block-room.png" width="1355" height="1800" alt="Wider view of the question-block light casting a warm yellow glow across the wall" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>A little extra atmosphere for the room.</figcaption></figure></div>
        </article>
        <article class="creation-showcase creation-showcase-reverse" id="geometric-tiger" aria-labelledby="tiger-title">
          <figure class="creation-media"><picture><source srcset="/assets/creations/geometric-tiger-magnet.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/assets/creations/geometric-tiger-magnet.png" width="1600" height="1205" alt="Geometric tiger magnetic sticker with raised purple and gold facets on a dark surface" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>Purple, gold, and a little geometric personality.</figcaption></figure>
          <div class="creation-copy"><p class="eyebrow">04 / TEAM SPIRIT</p><h3 id="tiger-title">LSU pride.<br><em>A different angle.</em></h3><p>A geometric tiger magnetic sticker for showing off LSU pride. Raised purple and gold facets give the familiar tiger silhouette texture, depth, and a look of its own.</p><p>I hope to grow this into a collection of designs for different sports teams that people can order. Have a team or color combination in mind? I’d love to hear about it.</p><a class="text-link" href="/#contact">Ask about a team design <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap future-work" id="heygears" aria-labelledby="heygears-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">COMING SOON / FULL COLOR 3D CREATIONS</p><h2 id="heygears-title">Your ideas.<br>In <em>full color.</em></h2></div>
      <div>
        <p class="large-copy">Personal moments, favorite characters, and one-of-a-kind designs—brought to life.</p>
        <p>I’m preparing to offer custom full-color 3D creations you can display, gift, and make your own. Imagine bride-and-groom figurines modeled after you for your wedding cake, your kids in their sports outfits, a family photo turned into a miniature scene, or a keepsake of a beloved pet.</p>
        <p>Your favorite MMO character could step off the screen and onto your shelf. Tabletop miniatures, collectible figures, detailed busts, tiny vehicles, and custom display scenes open up even more ways to bring an imagined world into the real one.</p>
        <p>The possibilities reach beyond figurines: architectural models, product concepts, colorful home decorations, raised artwork, and pieces that combine color with clear or translucent details. I’m also exploring custom surface printing for personalized phone cases, acrylic signs, coasters, and textured designs, plus graphics for mugs, T-shirts, hoodies, and tote bags.</p>
        <p>These services are coming soon. I’m developing the designs and production workflows, and I’ll share finished examples, available options, and ordering details as each offering is ready. Have something else in mind? Tell me your idea and we can explore what’s possible.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/#contact">Tell me your creation idea <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section shirt-section" id="custom-shirts" aria-labelledby="shirts-title">
      <div class="wrap creation-showcase">
        <figure class="creation-media"><picture><source srcset="/assets/creations/team-albedo-shirt-concept.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/assets/creations/team-albedo-shirt-concept.png" width="766" height="1024" alt="Black Team Albedo T-shirt mockup with a purple, gold, and white gothic wedding illustration" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>A concept for a shirt I plan to make for myself.</figcaption></figure>
        <div class="creation-copy"><p class="eyebrow">COMING LATER / CUSTOM T-SHIRTS</p><h2 id="shirts-title">An idea.<br>Your <em>favorite tee.</em></h2><p>I’m also planning to make custom T-shirts: another way to turn a personal idea into something you can wear.</p><p>This Team Albedo gothic wedding concept is one I plan to make for myself. The mockup shows how the artwork could look on a black shirt; it’s a personal project concept, with a finished shirt still to come.</p><p>I’ll share more designs and details about custom shirt requests as this side of the work develops.</p><a class="text-link" href="/#contact">Talk about a shirt idea <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="collection-contact wrap" aria-labelledby="creation-contact-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">HAVE SOMETHING IN MIND?</p><h2 id="creation-contact-title">Let’s make it <em>real.</em></h2><p>A custom part, a personal keepsake, a shirt idea, or something just for you. Tell me what you’re thinking.</p></div>
      <a class="button button-gold" href="/#contact">Discuss a creation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter article/>
</BaseLayout>
